Title: Everyone Here Is Happy
Credit: Opening short based on the story map by
Author: Josh
Draft date: October 16, 2026
Notes: Proposed five-minute opening only. Ends with Ethan's arrival in the Playways. New prop and dialogue details remain draft choices.

INT. INDOOR PLAY CENTRE - DAY

A birthday party in full swing. Paper plates. Crooked candles. The uneven percussion of children who have been told to clap.

ETHAN sits at the edge of it with a paper cup of coffee. He presses two fingers to his temple.

A paper crown drops over his eyes.

SARAH, four, stands on the seat beside him, pleased with her work. A yellow plastic star hangs from her wrist.

He lifts the crown just enough to see her.

ETHAN
Is that better?

She adjusts it. Worse. He holds very still while she considers him.

Sarah laughs. Ethan does too, quietly.

Across the room, children climb into a ball pit beneath a mesh climbing frame.

Sarah slides down from the seat. Taps the edge of the table twice.

SARAH
You say ready.

Ethan takes off the crown and leaves it on the table.

ETHAN
Ready.

She hops over a colored line in the carpet. Turns to see if he saw.

He gives her a small, solemn nod. An excellent jump.

His phone vibrates beside the coffee.

LENA: Mark and I can collect her if you're not up to it.

Ethan looks at the message. Starts a reply. Stops.

Sarah is at the ball-pit rail now.

SARAH
Dad. Watch this one.

ETHAN
One second.

He looks down again.

At the rail: two little taps.

Sarah climbs in.

INT. INDOOR PLAY CENTRE - BALL PIT - CONTINUOUS

Sarah wades through the balls toward a foam stepping block.

A larger child gets there first. Sarah reaches for the block.

The child pulls it away.

Sarah drops backward into the balls. An angry, frightened cry.

Ethan's head comes up.

He puts the phone face down and stands.

ETHAN
Hey. I'm here.

Sarah pushes one hand up through the bright surface.

The balls shift. Her hand disappears.

Ethan reaches the rail. Looks for the place she will come up.

Nothing.

He steps over.

INT. INDOOR PLAY CENTRE - BALL PIT - MOMENTS LATER

Ethan pushes balls aside. Her name, once, in the tone that usually brings her back.

ETHAN
Sarah.

A child points somewhere else. He checks there. Checks the first place again.

A STAFF MEMBER reaches the rail.

STAFF MEMBER
Everybody out for a moment, please.

Children climb past. The surface settles around Ethan.

ETHAN
She was right here.

He searches with both hands. Feels the padded bottom. Looks beneath the foam block.

The staff member speaks into a radio, already moving around the outside.

STAFF MEMBER
Check the far exit, please. Little girl. Blue top.

Ethan kneels lower.

Something yellow between his fingers.

Sarah's star. Its wrist loop has come loose.

He holds it only long enough to recognize it. Puts it in his pocket.

In the back corner, a few balls roll through a crease between two padded wall panels.

Ethan pushes his hand into it.

His whole forearm goes in.

He leans farther. His fingers find nothing behind the wall.

ETHAN
Sarah?

He looks up toward the staff member, who is checking the mesh on the far side.

Then back to the opening.

He lowers his face to it.

INT. PADDED PASSAGE - CONTINUOUS

The birthday room is still audible behind him.

Ethan pulls one shoulder through. Then the other.

Soft material presses close on both sides. His hand reaches forward. Finds a surface. He crawls.

The party becomes muffled. A voice calls from behind, too blurred to make out.

Ethan pauses. Turns his head as far as the space permits.

No view of the room.

Ahead, a small patch of warm light.

He reaches toward it.

The surface gives under his palm.

He slides.

INT. PLAYWAYS - ARRIVAL BASIN

Ethan lands on a padded slope and rolls into a shallow drift of colored balls.

He lies still. Takes a breath.

The birthday party has stopped.

He gets up on one elbow. Looks behind him.

A short tube mouth. Nothing beyond its bend.

He rises.

Only now do we see what he sees.

Bridges cross an enormous open space. Play tubes thread between bright platforms. Small doors stand at the ends of staircases that seem to hang in the air.

All of it softly lit. All of it waiting to be used.

Ethan takes a few steps, trying to find the edge of the room.

There is no edge he can see.

ETHAN
Sarah!

His voice travels a long way.

He takes the yellow star from his pocket. Looks at it. Closes his hand.

A pleasant arrival chime.

VENUE VOICE (V.O.)
Welcome. We're glad you're here.

A line of lights comes on along a path leading away from the basin.

Ethan looks back once at the tube mouth.

Then he turns toward the path.

His first step.

CUT TO BLACK.

EVERYONE HERE IS HAPPY

The sound of the Playways continues.

END
